00:00:02,664 --> 00:00:05,328
跟读：A Different Working Week.

3
00:00:05,328 --> 00:00:28,056
听：Leah manages a small design team. During a busy month, several employees asked for more autonomy. They wanted to choose where they worked on two days each week. Leah was interested in the proposal, but she worried about communication and the quality of customer service.

4
00:00:28,056 --> 00:00:50,784
跟读：Leah manages a small design team. During a busy month, several employees asked for more autonomy. They wanted to choose where they worked on two days each week. Leah was interested in the proposal, but she worried about communication and the quality of customer service.

5
00:00:50,784 --> 00:01:16,536
听：If the team works remotely, it will need a clear schedule. Leah therefore arranged a trial rather than making a permanent promise. If everyone worked different hours, meetings would be difficult to organise. She asked each employee to explain which tasks required collaboration and which could be done independently.

6
00:01:16,536 --> 00:01:42,288
跟读：If the team works remotely, it will need a clear schedule. Leah therefore arranged a trial rather than making a permanent promise. If everyone worked different hours, meetings would be difficult to organise. She asked each employee to explain which tasks required collaboration and which could be done independently.

7
00:01:42,288 --> 00:02:10,152
听：After six weeks, productivity had improved on some tasks, but the workload was not shared equally. One colleague felt isolated, while another enjoyed avoiding the daily journey. Their supervisor introduced a short morning meeting and a weekly mentoring session. The team began to judge progress by results rather than time online.

8
00:02:10,152 --> 00:02:38,016
跟读：After six weeks, productivity had improved on some tasks, but the workload was not shared equally. One colleague felt isolated, while another enjoyed avoiding the daily journey. Their supervisor introduced a short morning meeting and a weekly mentoring session. The team began to judge progress by results rather than time online.

9
00:02:38,016 --> 00:03:04,200
听：Leah concluded that flexibility needed boundaries. Employees had to remain available during agreed hours, although they could plan the rest of the day themselves. Higher job satisfaction was a welcome outcome, but no single arrangement suited everyone. The team agreed to review the trial before extending it.

